      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>WEDNESDAY, 22zio NOVEMBER,</head>
        <p>WEDNESDAY, 22zio NOVEMBER,</p>
        <p>PUBLIC MISSIONARY MEETING IN nix MEMORIAL HALL (Edgeworth it.), at 730. Speakers: REV. C. COLLINS, from Madagascar, and REV. W. C. WILLOUGHBY, South Africa. Collections on behalf of the Loudon Missionary Society.</p>
        <p>ROYAL COURT THEATRE, WARRINGTON. Puornirmn : MR. JOSEPH BEECHAM. GENERAL MANAGER: MR. A. M. LOADER. ACTING MANAGER: MR. H. WARBURTON. MONDAY, NOVEMBER 20TH, 1911, FOR Six NIGHTS MR. HENRY RENODF PRESENTS "TRILBY,"</p>
        <p>An Adaptation from GEORGE DU MAURIER'S Famous Novel. Fascinating. Humorous. Thrilling. Weird. The Piece will be played by • Carefully Selected Company including— MR. HENRY RENOUF as " Sveogali." and MISS NORAH VAUGHAN an "Trilby." The Play Produced by MR. HENRY RENOUF. Nest Week :—" The Prince and the Begget Maid." ARRIX T 0 N CHURCH SOCIETY</p>
        <p>JOSEPH CROSFIELD &amp; SON, LIMITED. 4; per cent. First Mortgage Irredeemable Debenture Stock. . .</p>
        <p>The Transfer Books of this Company, relative to this issue will be CLOSED from the 17th to the 30th November inst. (both days inclusive for the purpose of preparing and issuing Interest Warrants doe Ist December.</p>
        <p>November 16tb, 1 911,</p>
        <p>Signed 3. IL WARDLE, Secretary.</p>
        <p>NATIONAL UNION OF WOMEN'S SUFFRAGE SOCIETIES. . NON-PARTY. NON-MILITANT. There will be a PUBLIC MEETING at the DRILL HALL, FRODSHAM, on WEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 29th, 8.15 p.m. SPEAKERS :—The LADY FRANCES BALFOUR. Miss DEAKIN. CHAIRMAN :—Miu RATHBONE. W ARRINGTON INFIRMARY AND DISPENSARY CONTRACTS. The Board of Management invite TENDERS for WINDOW CLEANING, also for the supply of the following gr.ods, for the twelve months ending the 81st December, 1912 :—Drugs, Dressings, Groceries, Provisions, Household and Laundry Stores, Soda Water in 40oz. syphons, Poultry and Fish, Butchers' Meet, good Seconds Broad and Flour, and Milk. Persons tendering will be ',tithed to deliver the goods at the Infirmary free of cost, how and when required. The Board do not pledge themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. Forms of tender on application to the Secretary. Sealed tenders, addressed to the Chairman, to be delivered at the Infirmary by Thursday, the 30th November, 1911, J. H. J. HAMPSON, Secretary._ CIOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— The SANITARY WORKS COMMITTEE are prepared to SECOND-HANDreceive TGEANRDEBRASGsf,orIee s 00 zperilinogf 38ins. by 28ins. to hold*iwts.each,and 2,000 measuring Mins. by 241 n,. to hold ?cwt. each, to be delivered at Longford Depot at the rate of not less than 1,300 per week, deliveries to commence lot January, 1912. Samples may be seen and all further information obtained from the undersigned. Sample bags to be submitted along with tender, and any bag which is not equal in every respect to sample will be rejected. Tenders in securely fastened envelopes endorsed "Tender for Bags" and addressed Die Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington," to be delivered not later than Monday, 27th November, 1911. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. R. WILSON, Manager.</p>
        <p>Longford Depot, Warrington. 15th Novi=ler, 1911.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. EDUCATION COMMITTEE. TENDERS FOR ELECTRIC BELL INSTALLATION. TENDERS are invited for the ELECTRIC BELL INSTALLATION at the EVELYN STREET COUNCIL SCHOOL. Specifications may be obtained from the undersigned. Tenders must he forwarded, in the envelope pro- vided, by not later than noon on Friday, the lit December, 1911, to Education Office, J. MOORE MURRAY, M.Sc., Warrington. Stcretary and Director. 16th November, 1911. ciOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINOTON. ELECTRICITY DEPARTMENT. The ELECTRICITY and TRAMWAYS COM MITTER of the Corporation of Warrington are prepared to receive TENDERS for the supply of SLACK. Specification and Form of 'Tender can be obtained from the undersigned on payment of One Guinea, which will be returned on receipt of • bona-fide tender. Five shillings will be charged for extra copies of specification. Tenders, addressed to the "Chairman of the Elec. tricity and Tramways Committee, Town Hall, Warring- ton " must be iealed with wax and endorsed k Tender for Slack," sod delivered not later than 12 o'clock noon on Tuesday, November 281 h, 1911. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted.</p>
        <p>F. V. 1,. MATHIAS, Borough Electrical &amp; Tramways &amp;termer. Howley, Warrington. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRUGTON ELECTRICITY DEPARTMENT.</p>
        <p>The Electricity end Tramways Committee of the County Borough of Warrington are prepared to receive TENDERS for LOW TENSION CABLE. • • • • •</p>
        <p>Specification and form of Tender can be obtained from the undersigned on payment of one guinea, which will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Five shillings will be charged for extra copies of Specification. Tenders, addressed to the "Chairman of the Electri- city and Tramways Committee, Town Hall,Warrington," most be sealed with wax and endorsed "Tender for Low Tension Cable," and delivered not later than 12 o'clock noon on Tuesday, November 28th, 1911. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily he accepted. F. V. L MATHIAS, Borough Electrical and Tramways Engineer. Howley, Warrington.</p>
        <p>ANTHRACITE STOVES.</p>
      </div>
