        <head>COULD NOT SLEEP FOR ITCHING.</head>
        <p>COULD NOT SLEEP FOR ITCHING.</p>
        <p>" For eight months I safftred from a bad form of eczema all over my neck and arms. I could get no sleep for the itching and irritation. I was worn out. After tr3irg all kinds of remedies without avail, my hopes begun to sink, thinking I should not recover from the terrible malady. It would make its appear- ance all at once in small patches like pimples, accom- panied by itching and burning, and hooting for some few month., gradually getting better. Finally, in a short space of time, it would become much worse. It formed in red patches which disapreared upon its decline, leaving me at times very low and depressed and reduced me to a pitiful weakness. I had terrible headaches with a sickly feeling all over me, and would be subject to a sudden cold chill, which would follow after burning sensations in the daytime. At night I could get n rest, and the torture was indescribable. After having advice from a woman who had suffered the same, I resolved to try the Cutietwa treatment. I tried a little Cuticnra Ointment, sod got ease from it speedily, so I bought a tablet of Cuticurs Soap and a box of Cutictira Ointment, and I soon found myself improving. One cannot speak too highly of the wonderful treatment which completely cured me, and has restored me to perfect health. I shall surely recommend them wherever I am. My holier also suffered from eczema, and he reaped the same benefit as myself, lie says it is a most wonderful cure." (Signed) Miss Gertrude Turner, 2, Douglas St., Deptford, London, SE November 25, PM. Post- free, from F. Newbery &amp; Sons, 27, Charterhouse Sq., London, samples of Cuticura Soap and Ointment with 32-p. book on skin treatment.</p>
