        <p>A return laid before the Cheshire Education Com- mittee on Monday gave thecost of elementary education in Cheshire during the last school year. The total amount spent was £222,450, towards which nearly £120,000 was contributed by the Board of Education in grants, and £99,089 by the county rates. The principal items of expenditure core :—Salaries of teachers L1G1,610, salaries of teachers in spools! subjects £3,929, books, apparatus, pictures, stationery, Sic. £11,152, fuel, light, and cleaning £10,977, medical examinations of school children and Federica of medical officers and nurses .£1,i67, maintenance of defective children £1,904, selincies, Ac, of 2fi school attendance officers £2,.38. It was announced that Judge J. K. Bradbury had' I resigned his membership of the Committee. Much regret was expressed, and a resobilion was adopted recording Ids ser•ices to the Committee. Ills greetest : interest was in the Children's Care Committee and the employment bureau for children stout to leave school. Mr. George Rhodes, K.O , of the .Altrincham district, was appointed to succeed him.</p>
