      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <head>MR. HAROLD SMIFH, M P., ASKS QUESTIONS. Petrol for Ambulances.</head>
        <p>MR. HAROLD SMIFH, M P., ASKS QUESTIONS. Petrol for Ambulances.</p>
        <p>In the House of Commons on Monday, Mr. Harold Smith (U., Warrington) asked the Chsncellor of the Exchequer whether he hid received communications from Manchester asking for • rebate of the tax respect of petrol used by motor embolances used for the conveyance of the poor to and (rim the various Infirmaries, and whether he would take steps to insure that such rebate was granted. Mr. M'liinnon Wood said the answer to the first part was in the affirmative. The rebate in respect of motor spirit for ambulances was not pr tvided for order the existing law. The Chancallor of the FAL:hyper would consider whether the law on the subject could be amended.</p>
