      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0048" n="art0048">
        <head>AN OLD "WIREPULLER " AND FRIENDS ABROAD.</head>
        <p>AN OLD "WIREPULLER " AND FRIENDS ABROAD.</p>
        <p>The" Examiner" is kindly remembered in some strange quarters of the globe, and we print above a photo group of Warrington lads taken Stanley Park, Vencouver, Biitish Columbia, with a huge tree as background. The photo is sent by W. Barrett, an old Warrington Rugby forward, who will be easily recognised as fifth from the left in the top row. No doubt many of our readers will find friends in the group.</p>
