      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0049" n="art0049">
        <head>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</p>
        <p>1 WARRINGTON "A " Wctt. BEATEN.—At Wigan on Saturday, the home team had all the best of the game. Lloyd was prominent on the Warrington side in the early stages, but when Grven got away for Wigan Jordan tackled him after he had punted, and the referee awarded a try. Daintith made a fine run for Warring- ton, but again were the finishing touches lacking. Shallcross next scrambled over, Seddon missing the goal-kick. The locals forced the pace to advantage I and Careen sent Holding ovar for a good try, Shall- cross landing a goal. Grimshaw next troubled the defence, and after Jordan had been bustled off the ball J. H. Green scored for Shalicross to add another goal. Half-time Wigan, two goals four tries (IC points) ; Warrington, nil. In the second half, Povey and Clare both made good efforts, after nice combination, but were stopped a yard from the line. However, Daintith opened the scoring with a dropped goal, but Wigan soon got the upper band again. Superior combination brought tries in rapid succession to Shallcross, Taylor, Curwen (2) and Grimshaw, the final score being : Wigan 3 goals 9 tries (33 points) to Warrington 1 goal (2 pointa).</p>
      </div>
