        <p>RELAXES' RECRIATION V. CASTLE P.UDI:ER.—The Castle Rubber team were entertained at Rylands' Pavilion, Gorsey-lane, on Saturday, a most enjoyable evening being being spent. Thl most interesting game of the evening was that between Mr Mather and Mr H Maddock, the home cueist claiming the margin of one point to his credit After the match about GO partook of refreshments when Mr. H. Maddock La. Rylands' welcomed tbe visitors, commenting on the good feeling which existed among the various workmen in the town. Mr. T. Reddish supported. Mr. Burdett, responding on behalf of the Castle Rubber Works, made reference to the keen and enthusiastic way that the games had been played. Mr. T. O'Brien supported and a return match was arranged. Scores :</p>
