      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0072" n="art0072">
        <p>Liverpool Curate for Warrington.</p>
        <p>The Rev G A Coupe, cura.e of All Saints' Church, Great Nelson-street, Liverpool, will terminate his ministry no far as that church is conzerned about Chri• tunas, and will take up a curacy at St. &amp;unitises '.3llnrch, Warrington, under the lt,v J II G }lolling- worth, MA. Mr Coupe, who is a very young clergyman, commtnced his ministerial work about two years ago, at All Saints', having been previously ordained by the Bishop of Liverpool. His vicar (Rev W Thatcher) has I admittedly found In him a very able colleague. He is regarded (says a Liverpsol correspondont) as the ohildren's friend, and is an enthusiast in the Boys' Brig uzle movement.</p>
