        <p>Mother Seigel's Syrup is a perfect family medicine. It is a sure remedy because the curative extracts of which it is made tone up the stomach and regulate the action of the liver and bowels as no other medicine does. It is a speedy remedy because it acts directly upon those organs, and 'lns quickly restores them to working order. It is a gentle herbal remedy, yet thorough in its action. Keep a bottle handy, and if you have any stomach or liver troubles— pains after eating, headaches, biliousness, constipation, sleeplessness or low spirits —Mother Seigel's Syrup will prove a sure, speedy and gentle cure.</p>
        <p>WORLD'S REMEDY</p>
        <p>"I bzgan to suffer from digestive troubles about April, 1910. I had s2vere stomach pains. More often than not, food returned as soon as I had eaten it. Even a food advertised for invalids I could not keep down. I had sick headaches and was nervous, low spirited and slept badly. "I consulted a doctor who told me I had severe stomach trouble, but ordinary medicine did me no good. "But after the first few doses of Mother Seigel's Syrup / kept down milk food, and within three weeks I could eat any food with relish. Mother Seigel's Syrup had cured me."—Mrs. B. Lovett, 2, Tuskar St., Greenwich. 29/4/SI. FOR</p>
