      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0141" n="art0141">
        <head>WARRINGTON BRIDGE.-FIRST STAGE IN THE METAMORPHOSIS.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON BRIDGE.-FIRST STAGE IN THE METAMORPHOSIS.</p>
        <p>Photo Tonge,</p>
        <p>THE TEMPORARY WOODEN FOOT-BRIDGE OPENED THIS WEEK. One of the difficulties of the bridge contractors is that they have to maintain the thoroughfare witholt reducing the area for passenger 3 and traffic, and as a preliminary to commencing any work on the old structure Hey hive been obliged to throw across, on cantilevers, a tempOrary wooden foot-bridge on the east side of the Bridge. This fcot-bridge was opened on Thursday evening. The wall and parapet to the right of the picture will be removed at an early date to facilitate the work of the contractors.</p>
