        <p>BULL CHARGES BRIDAL PARTY.</p>
        <p>A bridal party was returning from tbe church at Brougb, Westmoreland, when a large ball, which was piing led gioeg the road, took fright at the crowd of sightseers, becks loose from the man in charge, and dashed straight at the assembleS people. Several women and children were knocked down, and a young married woman named Deightoa bed her collar-bone broken in endea•onring to save her child.</p>
